<Base description="Turning feedback into scoped automation work, with an interactive fictional backlog." title="Vantage"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/projects/">← Projects</a></p><h1>Vantage</h1><p class="intro">A place for ideas to become scoped work. Browse a sample backlog, open a brief, and explore the stages.</p><h2>From feedback to a backlog</h2><p>The published Rewst case study describes how the team gathered feedback and used Vantage to build an automation backlog. This demo illustrates that progression: capture the problem, name an owner, scope the work, and define how it will be reviewed.</p><p>Open a card to inspect its brief and move it to the next stage. These sample briefs are illustrative, not exported production records.</p><h2>Design choices</h2><p>An idea needs more than a title to become useful work. The brief puts the problem, owner, scope, and review criteria together so the next stage has something concrete to build on.</p><p class="meta">Interactive replica of my work · Fictional data · Selected interactions</p><p><a href="/demos/vantage/">Open full-screen ↗</a></p><iframe class="demo-frame" src="/demos/vantage/" title="Vantage interactive replica" loading="lazy"></iframe><p><a href="/years/2026/">The team’s automation process and published case study →</a></p></Base>